  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...While oceanside impacts along the Outer Banks\nhave lessened, minor soundside flooding continues. Will replace\nCF Warning with Advisory and continue into Sat morning, though\nthe main threat will be through late this evening. Long period \nswells continue to run higher than wave guidance and will \ncontinue High Surf Advisory into this afternoon for Hatteras \nIsland, Ocracoke Island and East Carteret (for Core Banks). \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Drying, cool, and relatively \"calmer\" \nconditions expected across ENC through the first half of the \nweekend ahead of the next front to cross the area late SUN \nnight/early MON morning with a secondary reinforcing front to \nfollow shortly thereafter. This poses the next best chance for \nrain with advertised NBM PoPs>90%. QPF however is minimal due \nto the much lower available moisture (compared to the Turkey Day\nstorm) and quick progression of the front; highest rainfall \namounts on the order of a tenth of an inch. All liquid precip \nexpected with temps in the low 60s ahead of the front and upper \n40s behind it. Prefrontal winds may flirt with wind advisory \ncriteria for portions of the immediate coast (OBX from Lookout \nto Oregon Inlet). Calmer, cooler, and clearer behind these \nfronts through midweek with MaxTs ~60 and MinT ~freezing inland,\nmid-upper 40s/low 50s coast through midweek.",
